 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6">Magazines</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Rob's brilliant cartoon on today's edition of The Sun.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P align=center><STRONG>FIRST PUBLISHED ON A MADONNA WEBSITE</STRONG></P>
<P align=justify>As you can see below, <STRONG><A href="http://www.thesun.co.uk/article/0,,4-2004470420,00.html" target=_blank>The Sun</A></STRONG> has published the brilliant cartoon penned by the very talented <STRONG>Rob Jacobs</STRONG>&nbsp;from <STRONG><A href="http://www.madonnamad.com" target=_blank>MadonnaMad.com</A></STRONG> that we showed you yesterday. 
<P align=center><STRONG>From today's edition of The Sun:</STRONG> 
<P align=center><IMG src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004470252,00.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><EM>Madge of honour ... leaving <BR>with husband Guy <BR>Picture: MATRIX</EM> <BR></P>
<P align=justify>THERE’S nothing trickier than going to a showbiz dinner just days after your lover has insulted the guest of honour. <BR><BR>So step forward ELTON JOHN’s partner DAVID FURNISH — the most red-faced man at DONATELLA VERSACE’s party for pal MADONNA. <BR><BR>Elt sparked a storm at last week’s Q Awards when Madge was nominated for Best Live Act and in a foul-mouthed tirade he accused her of miming. <BR><BR>So presumably he didn’t fancy showing his face at her party in posh London diner Cipriani on Thursday night — and gave David the job. <BR><BR>Certainly, David looked a little uneasy as he arrived and sat himself on a table as far away as possible from Madonna and her husband GUY RITCHIE. </P>
<P align=center><IMG src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004470243,00.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><EM>Frosty atmosphere ... David Furnish <BR>puts on brave face</EM> <BR></P>
<P align=justify>Security at the bash was tight but I sneaked one of my Bizarre team into the dinner — and he reports: “When David arrived you could tell he was quaking in his boots. <BR><BR>“Elton’s just lucky that he had a sacrificial lamb to send to the slaughter. There was an uncomfortable atmosphere and there were lots of intense stares coming from Madonna’s table.” <BR><BR>Publicly, Madge — who was not at the Q Awards — took Elt’s dig in good spirit and denied miming. She later joked he’d still be on her Christmas card list. <BR><BR>And fans who saw the Re-Invention gigs know she sang brilliantly live. She only mimed a few times — such as while doing the yoga crab pose on stage. <BR><BR><STRONG>And now Rob Jacobs, a Madonna fan and artist at <A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com" target=_blank>drownedmadonna.com</A>, has penned a brilliant cartoon asking tubby old Elton whether he could sing live while doing the crab.</STRONG> <BR><BR></P>
<P align=center><IMG src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004470246,00.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><EM>Quite a stretch ... Elton in cartoon</EM> <BR></P>
<P align=justify><STRONG>I’ve printed it above so you can all have a laugh.</STRONG> <BR><BR>Also at Donatella’s bash were LIZ HURLEY, JAMELIA and GEORGE MICHAEL’s lover KENNY GOSS. <BR><BR>They all had a great time. As did Madonna — despite the Elton row. <BR><BR></P>
<P align=center><IMG src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004470262,00.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><EM>Brave front ... she’s a no-nonsense girl</EM> <BR></P>
<P align=justify>In fact Madge had such a good time she glared at waiting photographers as she left in case they snapped her looking a little worse for wear. <BR><BR>ELTON had far more important things to do than go to Donatella’s bash. <BR>He’s been busy recording with up-and-coming star LUCIE SILVAS for a BBC performance that will go out later this year. <BR><BR></P>
<P align=center><IMG src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004470247,00.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><EM>Hi-ho Silvas ... lone ranger Elton <BR>is recording with Lucie</EM> <BR></P>
<P align=justify>Lucie’s debut single, What You’re Made Of, was out this week – and it’s really making waves. </P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
