    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P class=head3><STRONG>By Maureen Coleman<BR></STRONG><A class=mailto href="mailto:mcoleman@belfasttelegraph.co.uk"><STRONG>belfasttelegraph.co.uk</STRONG></A></P><STRONG>08 October 2004</STRONG> 
<P>Am I the only person who <STRONG>wishes "Sir" Elton John would disappear - and take his pompous-looking prat of a boyfriend with him?</STRONG></P>
<P><STRONG>Having been in the pit area at Slane Castle this summer, to watch Madonna play her first gig in Ireland, I can honestly say she was definitely singing live and not merely lip-synching as the "Queen" of hissy fits proclaimed.</STRONG></P>
<P><STRONG>Madonna put on a first class</STRONG> all-dancing, all-singing show, which went down a storm with her fans.</P>
<P>In contrast, <STRONG>I watched Elton John in concert in Belfast and frankly, was bored to tears half way through the show.</STRONG></P>
<P><STRONG>Even if Madonna had been miming (which she wasn't) I know which performance I'd have rather seen.</STRONG></P>
</font></div>
