 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=14">Music</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Laura Pausini inteviewed by Mexican EXA FM.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG><IMG src="http://www.exafm.com.mx/imagescont/galerias/laura_entrevistaoct3.jpg" align=left border=0>Laura Pausini</STRONG> is currently on tour in <STRONG>Latin America</STRONG> promoting her upcoming album <STRONG>"Resta In Ascolto"</STRONG>. After being in <STRONG>Puerto Rico</STRONG>, she has visited <STRONG>Mexico</STRONG> and she has been interviewed by Mexican <STRONG>EXA FM</STRONG>. Here's an interesting&nbsp;excerpt&nbsp;regarding <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and the song -<STRONG> "Mi Abbandono A Te" / "Mi&nbsp;Abandono A Ti"</STRONG>&nbsp;(originally titled <STRONG>"Like A Flower"</STRONG>) - she gave her:</P>
<P><STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> wrote the last track of my disk that is called <STRONG>"Mi Abbandono A Te" /"Mi Abandono A Ti"</STRONG>.&nbsp;It's a song that I&nbsp;received about a&nbsp;year and a half ago. She gave it to me in English, but she wanted&nbsp;it to be sung by an interpreter that could sing it in another language... and I believe that&nbsp;she chose me&nbsp;because, aside from being able to sing it in Spanish, I can sing it in Italian, which is a language that she loves so much because of her Italian origins.&nbsp;</P>
<P>Working with her&nbsp;was very interesting, and&nbsp;even if I enterely worked on the song with the producer of <STRONG>The Power Of Good-Bye</STRONG> and some other songs&nbsp;from&nbsp;her&nbsp;<STRONG>Ray Of Light</STRONG> album,&nbsp;it&nbsp;has been completely recorded and arranged in <STRONG>London</STRONG> while she was on tour. However, she wanted to know every single thing.&nbsp;<STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> took care of what I wrote,&nbsp;because, translating it,&nbsp;I changed the whole meaning of the song. </P>
<P>It's not about&nbsp;the&nbsp;love-affair&nbsp;between a man and a woman, but it's about&nbsp;the inner peace of the people, just like if we are&nbsp;sat one in front of the other. It's a very spiritual song, and, compared to the first demo she sent me, it's quite different. </P>
<P>I like to work with someone this way,&nbsp;because only the biggest artists like her can respect contributions... leave you free... a little bit of her and a little of&nbsp;me... I think this is the true way to work... when two persons are united and at the same time&nbsp;very different musically, it's interesting to listen to&nbsp;their meeting... which is not&nbsp;necessarily one the adaptation of the other. </P>
<P>If I don't identify&nbsp;myself, I don't sing a song... even if it's written by a very important artist. I don't accept songs written by important people that don't let you change anything... don't let me feel myself identifing with the song. </P>
<P><EM>Translation by DrownedMadonna.</EM></P>
<P><A href="http://www.exafm.com.mx/entrevista.php?id=215" target=_blank>Click here</A> to read the whole interview for radio <STRONG>EXA FM</STRONG> on <STRONG>10/04/2004</STRONG>.</P>
<P align=center><IMG src="/images/2004/pausini2.jpg" border=0></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
