    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6">Magazines</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>More articles about Madonna's fans lashing back Elton John.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>From <STRONG><EM>eircom</EM> net</STRONG>:</P>
<P><STRONG>Madonna fans attack Elton</STRONG> <BR><BR>From: BANG Media International <BR>Wednesday, 06 October, 2004 <BR><BR>LONDON (BANG) - Elton John has been branded "senile" and "jealous" by outraged Madonna fans. <BR><BR>The sexy singer’s supporters are furious at the "bitchy" star for accusing her of miming when he accepted his Classic Songwriter prize at London’s Q Awards. <BR><BR>One angry fan fumed on Madonna website <STRONG><A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com">www.drownedmadonna.com</A></STRONG>: "Is he still alive? Or is he senile and getting Madonna mixed up with Britney Spears? Stick to writing cr*p tunes Elton and ditch your toupee - it’s the only thing alive on him!" <BR><BR>Another claimed Elton only made the vitriolic comments because he was jealous of Madonna’s success. <BR><BR>The fan wrote: "Elton John - what could you say about him? He has a silly name, writes bad songs and wears a wig and stupid specs. At least Madonna is a woman, not a fat frog. Madonna does not need too slag off other artists to keep her career alive. She just gets better and better. Sorry Elton, jealousy is a very big problem." <BR><BR>Another Madonna devotee also pointed out that Elton, who slammed Madonna for charging 75GBP-a-ticket to her ’re-Invention’ tour, also charged hefty ticket prices - up to $500 - for his Las Vegas shows. <BR><BR>(c) BANG Media International </P>
<P>
<HR>

<P></P>
<P>TV channel <STRONG>Five</STRONG> features the same article from <STRONG>ITV</STRONG> and <STRONG>Channel 4</STRONG>:</P>
<P><STRONG>Madonna fans lash back at Elton</STRONG> <BR>2004-10-06 16:42:22&nbsp;<BR><BR>Madonna’s legion of fans have launched a vigorous defence of the singer following Sir Elton John’s recent verbal assault. <BR><BR>Sir Elton’s expletive-strewn tirade against Madonna at the Q Awards accused the singer of miming in her concerts. <BR><BR>However, Madge’s friend Rupert Everett has waded into the war of words, accusing Elt of being "bossy and cranky". <BR><BR>And on Madonna’s website <STRONG><A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com" target=_blank>www.drownedmadonna.com</A></STRONG>, fans have lined up to criticise Elt, one of pop’s elder statesmen. They label him a "fat frog" and dub him senile. <BR><BR>Speaking about Madonna’s nomination for Best Live Act, Sir Elton said anyone who lip-synchs at a £75 per person concert "should be shot". <BR><BR>He said: "Madonna, best f****** live act? F*** off. Since when has lip-synching been live? That’s me off her f****** Christmas card list but do I give a toss? No." <BR><BR>A spokeswoman for Madonna said Sir Elton remains on the star’s Christmas card list "whether he is nice ... or naughty". </P>
</font></div>
